es tumor-type classification and localization from genomic data using a large language model; this is a predictive classification task with no generative mechanism mentioned.,,Large language models enable tumor-type classification and localization of cancers of unknown primary from genomic data,"while DNA methylation and transcriptomic profiling classify 75%  Second, expanding the  feature space to include multimodal data To enable training of the large language model (LLM),",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,application_wrapper,no,no,no,unclear,genomic data,none,tumor-type classification,clear_exclude,"The abstract only references genomic data and tumor-type classification, with no mention of natural-language text or generation. This indicates the LLM is used as a wrapper for a discriminative task, not as a new multimodal generative model.","The title describes a new LLM‑based approach for tumor‑type classification from genomic data, indicating a primary model paper with a biological modality, but the abstract lacks explicit mention of natural‑language text or a text‑bio mapping.","The title/abstract describe using a large language model for tumor-type classification and localization, with no mention of a generative mechanism; the work appears to apply an existing LLM to a downstream task.","The abstract only references genomic data and tumor-type classification, with no mention of natural-language text or generation. This indicates the LLM is used as a wrapper for a discriminative task, not as a new multimodal generative model.",Large language models enable tumor-type classification and localization of cancers of unknown primary from genomic data,"while DNA methylation and transcriptomic profiling classify 75%  Second, expanding the  feature space to include multimodal data To enable training of the large language model (LLM),",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,text_component_unclear,application_wrapper,unclear,unclear,no